It also largely nixes spellcasting ability.  They're very nice early
on, but I rarely find them to be worth a wish --e.g. wishing for the
blessed +3 grayswandir is likely to give you a lot more damage bonus
than wishing up the gauntlets, and you'll continue to use it later on
in the game when you're casting a lot (archaeologists are excellent
casters).  Keeping your spells at a low failure rate is pretty
important.

I almost always throw away the gauntlets right around the Quest/
Castle, as spellcasting is so powerful at that point.

For classes that can really machine-gun thrown weapons, the calculus
is a bit different; I still generally prefer to work on my
spellcasting in the long term, but early on the GoPower are very nice
indeed.  I guess if I had a wizard with multiple MR sources I'd
consider seeing if a robe + GoP were viable.

