An archaeologist dual-wielding is well into the "overkill" damage from
melee; much of that +600 is a complete waste.  It's really the average
hits/kill that you should be looking at--more specifically, the
average hits/kill on monsters that may present a danger.

I'd bet you're probably better off working on spellcasting , saving a
lot of turns (hence facing fewer monsters) mapping out Gehennom,
stacking up haste self (hence allowing jumping and still getting those
extra free attacks), skilled detect monsters (thus seeing them
approach and actually being able to _use_ those darts from 12 squares
away in the dark), etc.



